/P 81 0 R
/E (Tattva is aimed at a broad and diverse audience, exploring universal themes such as transformation, slowing down, rebuilding and identity. The performance invites both experienced performing arts audiences and those less familiar with performance to watch, listen and experience in an intuitive way. Through its open and sensory nature, Tattva is accessible to people of all ages and backgrounds.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
115 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 81 0 R
/E (The performance can take place both in theatres and cultural centres, as well as in unconventional locations such as historic buildings, industrial spaces or outdoor environments. What is essential is an intimate setting in which the audience and performers share the same space, without an overload of sensory stimuli.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
116 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 81 0 R
/E (The performance can also be combined with a workshop. During the workshop, participants are introduced to the themes explored in the performance. As a yoga teacher, Amber shares her knowledge and guides participants towards a deeper connection with their bodies. The experience is enriched by a soundscape created by Arnaud, who uses sound and music to support and deepen the experience.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [3]
>>
